**Technical Specification Document**

**Title:** Network Infrastructure and Spectrum Allocation for Urban Expansion

**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Prepared by:** Network Solutions Group, Inc.  

**Requirements:**  
1. **Network Infrastructure:** Implement a robust fiber optic backbone connecting the new data center at 123 Tech Park Drive, Austin, TX, to existing nodes in the AT&T network (Node ID: ATX-01) by December 31, 2024.  
2. **Mobile Coverage:** Collaborate with Verizon Wireless to enhance 5G coverage across downtown Austin, targeting an increase in user capacity by 30% within the next 12 months.   
3. **Spectrum Management:** Secure 80 MHz of C-band spectrum from the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) for deployment in the Austin area to facilitate increased mobile data traffic, with a review date set for January 15, 2024.

**Constraints:**  
- All installations must comply with IEEE 802.11 standards, and any fiber deployment must not interfere with existing systems operated by Comcast and T-Mobile in the vicinity.  
- Project dependencies include approval from the City of Austin Planning Department for infrastructure modifications by November 1, 2023, and coordination with the National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) regarding spectrum allocation feedback by November 15, 2023.  

**Details:**  
- The project will involve the integration of Cisco Nexus 9000 Series switches at the new data center, and coordination with Dell Technologies for server deployments will be necessary.  
- Ongoing monitoring and reporting will be conducted in partnership with the Austin Technology Council to assess user experience and network performance metrics bi-annually.  

**End of Document**